Feature: TC_08_STAFF - SIM Amendments Core and SIM Tick E2E Regression Pack

  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Legacy  : "Regression Suite for SIM Amendments" (BISSAGL-7110, AT-TC-01 to 04, tmslinks BISSAGL-14864/14862/14861/14860)
  #           "Regression Suite for SIM Tick Internal and INET" (BISSAGL-7578, AT-TC-01 to 05, tmslinks BISSAGL-14839/
  #           14838/14782/14781/14779) - this pack had no feature file in the new framework, so it is folded in here.
  # Rewritten 15-10-2026 in the StaffSteps vocabulary (the wording the MAPS features run with). One end-to-end
  # scenario; # SECTION markers show where each legacy scenario starts.
  #
  # Purpose:
  #   - amend the claimed area of a SIM parcel and save
  #   - the original application total stays visible after an amendment
  #   - the SIM opt-in toggle works from the SIM screen
  #   - the SIM tick on the BISS Application summary follows the SIM opt-in state, with a history entry each time,
  #     and the calculated payable area is shown before and after the change
  #
  # Legacy coverage notes carried forward:
  #   - BISSAGL-7110 AT-TC-03 only navigated to the SIM tab and stopped (legacy comment: "parcel with errors needed
  #     that can be cleared on Admin Inspection page" - the data was never created). It is not reproduced; the SIM
  #     tick sections give this pack real assertions instead.
  #   - BISSAGL-7110 AT-TC-04's body after the toggle was commented out in legacy; Section 3 ends at the toggle.
  #   - BISSAGL-7578 AT-TC-03 / 04 were retests of AT-TC-01 / 02 with the same herds; run once here.
  #
  # Test data (kept as literals, as in legacy):
  #   A1071109 (2024, parcel Y2031000006; and 2023 for the total and the toggle),
  #   D3670245 / 2023 (SIM opted IN - deselect test), D1591313 / 2023 (SIM opted OUT - select test), I122C514 / 2023.
  #   Login agr4442 (BISS Co-ordination 1). Password: TD:Password from the TestData row of this test case.
  #
  # Step definitions: stepdefinitions.BISS.STAFF.StaffSteps
  # Author: Aniket Pathare | aniket.pathare@government.ie
  # --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Background:
    Given the staff user is logged in to the BISS internal portal as "agr4442"

  @regression @staff @sim @e2e
  Scenario: AT-STAFF-SIM-CORE-E2E-01 - Staff amends a SIM parcel, checks the totals and the SIM tick on the summary

    # SECTION 1 : Amend the claimed area of a SIM parcel - BISSAGL-7110 AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14864)
    When the staff user has opened the SIM screen for herd "A1071109" for scheme year "2024"
    And the staff user amends SIM parcel "Y2031000006" with the following values
      | amendedClaimedArea | 2.25 |
    Then the SIM amendment should be saved

    # SECTION 2 : The original application total is still shown - BISSAGL-7110 AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14862)
    When the staff user has opened the SIM screen for herd "A1071109" for scheme year "2023"
    Then the original application total should be displayed

    # SECTION 3 : SIM opt-in toggle - BISSAGL-7110 AT-TC-04 (BISSAGL-14860)
    When the staff user has opened the SIM screen for herd "A1071109" for scheme year "2023"
    And the staff user toggles the SIM scheme option

    # SECTION 4 : Deselect SIM - the tick on the BISS Application summary follows - BISSAGL-7578 AT-TC-01 (BISSAGL-14839)
    # The tick is read first, so the check works whichever way the herd is opted when the run starts.
    When the staff user opens the application for herd "D3670245" for scheme year "2023"
    Then the SIM tick state should be readable on the BISS Application summary
    When the staff user changes the SIM opt-in and submits with note "Test Note for 8078"
    Then the amendment should be recorded in the application history
    And the SIM tick on the BISS Application summary should have changed
    When the staff user changes the SIM opt-in and submits with note "Reset Test for 8078"

    # SECTION 5 : Select SIM - the tick and the calculated payable area follow - BISSAGL-7578 AT-TC-02 (BISSAGL-14838)
    When the staff user opens the application for herd "D1591313" for scheme year "2023"
    Then the SIM tick state should be readable on the BISS Application summary
    When the staff user opens the "SIM" screen
    Then the calculated payable area should change with the SIM opt-in state
    When the staff user changes the SIM opt-in and submits with note "Test Note for 8079"
    Then the calculated payable area should change with the SIM opt-in state
    And the amendment should be recorded in the application history
    And the SIM tick on the BISS Application summary should have changed
    When the staff user changes the SIM opt-in and submits with note "Reset Test for 8079"

    # SECTION 6 : SIM tick check only - BISSAGL-7578 AT-TC-05 (BISSAGL-14779)
    When the staff user opens the application for herd "I122C514" for scheme year "2023"
    Then the SIM tick state should be readable on the BISS Application summary
